  "id": "t05-002",
  "track": "track-05",
  "title": "authentication versus authorization identities claims and roles",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "Authentication establishes an identity and principal from credentials; authorization evaluates whether that principal may perform an operation on a resource. Successful login does not grant universal permission.",
    "Claims are statements attached to an identity and may come from different issuers. Roles are one claim convention; policies and resource checks can combine facts about identity, operation, and object state.",
    "Authorization belongs at the server boundary for each protected operation. Hiding a button or trusting client-supplied role values is not enforcement.",
    "Tenant boundaries, least privilege, explicit default-deny policy, and revalidation after permission changes are essential to prevent cross-user and cross-tenant access."
  ],
